WEBVTT

00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:06.940
Lois, you've had a near-death experience.

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:07.940
You should be resting.

00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:09.939
What are we doing out here?

00:00:09.939 --> 00:00:12.939
I'm going to find out what Lex is up to.

00:00:12.939 --> 00:00:15.939
Clark, you on the other hand are not required to attend.

00:00:15.939 --> 00:00:20.940
After what happened to Lana, why don't you take up Chloe's offer and hang out with her to tell him?

00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:22.940
It's dangerous out here.

00:00:22.940 --> 00:00:25.940
And it seems that keeping you out of trouble has become a bad habit of mine.

00:00:25.940 --> 00:00:28.940
Besides, gives me a good opportunity to say goodbye.

00:00:28.940 --> 00:00:32.939
You can't break up with me, Clark. We're not even a couple.

00:00:32.939 --> 00:00:35.939
Lois, I'm leaving Smallville.

00:00:35.939 --> 00:00:37.939
After Lana's funeral.

00:00:37.939 --> 00:00:43.659
Wow, didn't see that coming.

00:00:43.659 --> 00:00:45.659
Where are you running away to?

00:00:45.659 --> 00:00:47.659
Up north.

00:00:47.659 --> 00:00:49.659
There's something I need to do.

00:00:49.659 --> 00:00:52.659
What about the farm? You can't just let the corn die on the vine.

00:00:52.659 --> 00:00:58.030
My neighbor, Ben Hubbard, he's going to run things for a while.

00:00:58.030 --> 00:01:01.030
What's wrong, Lois? I thought you'd be happy to get rid of me.

00:01:01.030 --> 00:01:03.030
Are you kidding? What am I going to pick on?

00:01:03.030 --> 00:01:08.659
I'm sure you'll find someone.

00:01:08.659 --> 00:01:10.659
Now, which direction did you enter the damn problem?

00:01:10.659 --> 00:01:24.310
Southeast, follow me.

00:01:24.310 --> 00:01:25.310
This is amazing!

00:01:25.310 --> 00:01:31.280
Check this out, Clark!

00:01:31.280 --> 00:01:34.280
Oh my god.

00:01:34.280 --> 00:01:36.280
What do you think this is?

00:01:36.280 --> 00:01:39.280
Well, this is probably just some sort of experimental airplane.

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:41.280
And why aren't there any windows?

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:43.280
And those symbols?

00:01:43.280 --> 00:01:47.280
They aren't like any airline logos I've ever seen.

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:51.280
If you ask me, we're looking at a real-life spaceship.

00:01:51.280 --> 00:01:53.280
Come on, Lois.

00:01:53.280 --> 00:01:55.280
You and I both know that they don't really exist.

00:01:55.280 --> 00:01:59.280
And based on this algae, it looks like it's been underwater for a while.

00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:16.650
That's what happens when you touch my stuff.

00:02:16.650 --> 00:02:33.500
Go get your girlfriend.

00:02:33.500 --> 00:02:36.500
And don't ever come back.

00:02:36.500 --> 00:04:27.800
You go to the hospital.

00:04:27.800 --> 00:04:30.800
For this little bump? My head has been bonked a lot harder than that.

00:04:30.800 --> 00:04:31.800
Where's my laptop?

00:04:31.800 --> 00:04:33.800
What happened to you guys?

00:04:33.800 --> 00:04:35.800
You were gonna want to lock me in the lanybin when I tell you this,

00:04:35.800 --> 00:04:40.399
but Clark and I just saw spaceship.

00:04:40.399 --> 00:04:43.399
Lois's imagination is finally kicked into overdrive.

00:04:43.399 --> 00:04:45.399
It was probably just some sort of styrofoam prop for a school play.

00:04:45.399 --> 00:04:46.399
for a school play.

00:04:46.399 --> 00:04:48.399
Right, that makes sense, actually.

00:04:48.399 --> 00:04:50.399
Okay, but the world I live in, school props,

00:04:50.399 --> 00:04:52.399
don't knock people unconscious.

00:04:52.399 --> 00:04:54.399
I'm thinking maybe a force field.

00:04:54.399 --> 00:04:56.399
How many times I'll have to tell you, Lois,

00:04:56.399 --> 00:04:58.399
you slipped in the mud, you hit your head on a rock?

00:04:58.399 --> 00:04:59.399
I was the one who helped you to your feet.

00:04:59.399 --> 00:05:01.399
Why do you think I've got mud all over me?

00:05:01.399 --> 00:05:02.399
I know what I saw, Smallville,

00:05:02.399 --> 00:05:03.399
and once I change out of these clothes,

00:05:03.399 --> 00:05:05.399
I'm going straight to the Inquisitor.

00:05:05.399 --> 00:05:09.899
My editor is gonna flip.

00:05:09.899 --> 00:05:10.899
Tell me, she's just seeing things.

00:05:10.899 --> 00:05:12.899
That's what she didn't see, Chloe.

00:05:12.899 --> 00:05:13.899
A Kryptonian girl,

00:05:13.899 --> 00:05:15.899
with blonde hair and a bad attitude.

00:05:15.899 --> 00:05:16.899
She moved so fast that Lois didn't even know what hit her.

00:05:16.899 --> 00:05:17.899
A cryptic.

00:05:17.899 --> 00:05:19.899
Cryptonian attacked Lois?

00:05:19.899 --> 00:05:21.899
Yeah, right before she came after me.

00:05:21.899 --> 00:05:25.899
Chloe, not only she's as strong as I am, she can fly.

00:05:25.899 --> 00:05:29.879
Sounds like we got ourselves a true blue supergirl.

00:05:29.879 --> 00:05:31.879
I'll define super.

00:05:31.879 --> 00:05:34.879
Nearly every kryptonian that I've come across has turned into a cold-blooded killer.

00:05:34.879 --> 00:05:36.879
Yeah, what is it with you people?

00:05:36.879 --> 00:05:39.879
Are you the only half-decent member of your Kryptonian race?

00:05:39.879 --> 00:05:42.879
Listen, I gotta go back to the dam.

00:05:42.879 --> 00:05:45.160
If you can...

00:05:45.160 --> 00:05:49.160
Wow, a lot of painkillers for someone who's not feeling any pain.

00:05:49.160 --> 00:05:51.160
It's just a little headache.

00:05:51.160 --> 00:05:54.160
By the time I get back to The Inquisitor, I'll be good as gold.

00:05:54.160 --> 00:05:55.160
You've lost consciousness.

00:05:55.160 --> 00:05:57.160
You could very well have a concussion.

00:05:57.160 --> 00:05:59.160
Well, I'll let you know if I'm seeing double when I'm typing my story.

00:05:59.160 --> 00:06:01.160
You know what, Lois? No, I'm sorry.

00:06:01.160 --> 00:06:03.160
But after everything we've just been through together,

00:06:03.160 --> 00:06:05.160
I'm not letting you put yourself in danger.

00:06:05.160 --> 00:06:06.160
I'm taking you to the hospital.

00:06:06.160 --> 00:06:11.939
But ten minutes and I'm gone.

00:06:11.939 --> 00:06:14.939
I don't have time to just sit around all day in a waiting room just for a...

00:06:14.939 --> 00:06:37.139
Oh, I'm glad someone has something to smile about.

00:06:37.139 --> 00:06:40.139
Well, this smile means that you've been cleared of all charges.

00:06:40.139 --> 00:06:45.949
You're a free man, Mr. Luther.

00:06:45.949 --> 00:06:46.949
What grounds?

00:06:46.949 --> 00:06:48.750
They caught the killer.

00:06:48.750 --> 00:06:51.050
A disgruntled employee from your tunnel construction crew

00:06:51.050 --> 00:06:54.649
claimed they got cancer from the chemicals down there.

00:06:54.649 --> 00:06:57.550
He blew up my wife to get back at me.

00:06:57.550 --> 00:07:00.949
That's what he said in his confession.

00:07:00.949 --> 00:07:04.110
Come on, let's get out of this cage.

00:07:04.110 --> 00:07:06.569
I'll buy you a big, juicy porterhouse.

00:07:06.569 --> 00:07:08.170
He didn't do it.

00:07:08.170 --> 00:07:09.670
Lax.

00:07:09.670 --> 00:07:11.610
They found his fingerprints at the scene.

00:07:11.610 --> 00:07:12.569
He confessed to the crime.

00:07:12.569 --> 00:07:14.970
I don't care what kind of evidence there is.

00:07:14.970 --> 00:07:16.449
The man did not murder my wife.

00:07:16.449 --> 00:07:17.449
As your attorney?

00:07:17.449 --> 00:07:21.449
As my attorney, I want you to set up a meeting with this disgruntled employee.

00:07:21.449 --> 00:07:23.449
I want to hear it from him.

00:07:23.449 --> 00:07:25.449
What's the point?

00:07:25.449 --> 00:07:28.449
I'm not sure Lana's dead.

00:07:28.449 --> 00:07:50.750
Move a lock, sir. This is a crime scene.

00:07:50.750 --> 00:08:28.199
Lex, I thought you'd be sharpening your shiv behind bars by now.

00:08:28.199 --> 00:08:30.199
Someone else can fast.

00:08:30.199 --> 00:08:35.200
Once again, a Luther snake manages to slither away from the grip of justice.

00:08:35.200 --> 00:08:37.200
How much do you have to pay this, poor guy?

00:08:37.200 --> 00:08:39.200
pay this poor guy.

00:08:39.200 --> 00:08:41.200
I didn't pay him anything.

00:08:41.200 --> 00:08:45.200
Apparently, my father did before he disappeared.

00:08:45.200 --> 00:08:48.200
A man who confessed happens to be dying of cancer.

00:08:48.200 --> 00:08:50.200
He wanted his family taken care of.

00:08:50.200 --> 00:08:53.200
Doesn't matter what legal sleight of hand you pulled this time, Lex.

00:08:53.200 --> 00:08:54.200
It's not bringing Lana back.

00:08:54.200 --> 00:08:56.200
What if she isn't dead, Chloe?

00:08:56.200 --> 00:08:58.200
Lex, you're already free.

00:08:58.200 --> 00:09:02.200
You don't need to keep coming up with more convoluted conspiracy theories.

00:09:02.200 --> 00:09:06.200
As you probably know, before Lana died, she managed to

00:09:06.200 --> 00:09:09.200
She managed to steal highly classified research from me.

00:09:09.200 --> 00:09:12.200
Lana's remains have all been positively IDed,

00:09:12.200 --> 00:09:14.200
down to every last strand of DNA.

00:09:14.200 --> 00:09:16.200
I'm well aware of the DNA evidence.

00:09:16.200 --> 00:09:19.200
Look, Chloe, you're Lana's best friend.

00:09:19.200 --> 00:09:21.200
If she told anyone about her plan, it would be you.

00:09:21.200 --> 00:09:28.259
Tell me, Chloe. Tell me everything you know.

00:09:28.259 --> 00:09:30.259
Here's everything I know, Lex.

00:09:30.259 --> 00:09:33.259
You need some serious psychiatry.

00:09:33.259 --> 00:09:51.549
Are you all right?

00:09:51.549 --> 00:09:52.549
Yeah, I'm fine.

00:09:52.549 --> 00:09:54.549
But you know, your little Kryptonian Gallup House

00:09:54.549 --> 00:09:55.549
has been showing up all over Lowell County.

00:09:55.549 --> 00:09:58.549
Lowell County. Have you seen her since she went all space shuttle?

00:09:58.549 --> 00:10:00.549
No, but I found her victims.

00:10:00.549 --> 00:10:03.549
Two dead park rangers right where her ship used to be.

00:10:03.549 --> 00:10:08.049
I need to find her before she hurt someone else.

00:10:08.049 --> 00:10:12.049
Well, I think she's still grounded considering these nine-one-one-one calls coming in.

00:10:12.049 --> 00:10:17.049
Three different preschools called and reported some blonde woman storming and scaring the children.

00:10:17.049 --> 00:10:19.049
Where was she last seen?

00:10:19.049 --> 00:10:29.970
What's your name?

00:10:29.970 --> 00:10:35.600
It's okay. I don't hurt you.

00:10:35.600 --> 00:10:37.600
Cody?

00:10:37.600 --> 00:10:45.480
What about you?

00:10:45.480 --> 00:10:46.480
What's your name?

00:10:46.480 --> 00:10:49.720
Whatever you're doing, it stops now.

00:10:49.720 --> 00:10:51.720
Hey again.

00:10:51.720 --> 00:11:02.360
Following me? Humans can't move that fast.

00:11:02.360 --> 00:11:04.360
Who are you?

00:11:04.360 --> 00:11:05.360
It doesn't matter.

00:11:05.360 --> 00:11:08.360
I'm not going to let you kill one more person.

00:11:08.360 --> 00:11:10.360
I haven't killed anyone.

00:11:10.360 --> 00:11:12.360
At least not yet.

00:11:12.360 --> 00:11:14.360
But you're starting to tempt me.

00:11:14.360 --> 00:11:27.409
You want to tell me what you're doing on Earth?

00:11:27.409 --> 00:11:32.090
You can trust me.

00:11:32.090 --> 00:11:40.679
Looking for a small boy.

00:11:40.679 --> 00:11:43.679
I've searched everywhere with no luck.

00:11:43.679 --> 00:11:47.799
Spoil the name?

00:11:47.799 --> 00:11:48.799
Kala.

00:11:48.799 --> 00:12:01.049
Lois, a story about a spaceship is not going to send your career into the stratosphere.

00:12:01.049 --> 00:12:03.049
It'll embarrass you.

00:12:03.049 --> 00:12:05.049
It's the truth, Chloe. I saw it with my own eyes.

00:12:05.049 --> 00:12:07.049
Lois, you don't know what you saw.

00:12:07.049 --> 00:12:09.049
Besides, I'm still trying to resuscitate my credibility

00:12:09.049 --> 00:12:12.049
after writing about the Smallville, believe it or not, set.

00:12:12.049 --> 00:12:15.049
We are talking about an alien invasion.

00:12:15.049 --> 00:12:17.049
Two men are dead. You know, if you were there,

00:12:17.049 --> 00:12:19.049
you'd be clacking away on the keyboard as we speak.

00:12:19.049 --> 00:12:20.049
Not now.

00:12:20.049 --> 00:12:24.049
The Daily Planet just hired a new editor Wonderboy from the Star City Post,

00:12:24.049 --> 00:12:26.049
and spaces are not the stuff of good first impressions.

00:12:26.049 --> 00:12:27.049
Did I?

00:12:27.049 --> 00:12:29.049
someone say spaceship?

00:12:29.049 --> 00:12:32.049
Didn't anyone teach you that eavesdropping is rude?

00:12:32.049 --> 00:12:34.049
Eavesdropping is my livelihood.

00:12:34.049 --> 00:12:36.049
Grant Gabriel, your new editor.

00:12:36.049 --> 00:12:39.049
Actually, she doesn't work here. I do. I'm Chloe.

00:12:39.049 --> 00:12:43.049
Anne Sullivan, former editor of the Smallville High Torch,

00:12:43.049 --> 00:12:46.049
taking Met You journalism classes by night while writing

00:12:46.049 --> 00:12:50.049
filler stories, sandwiched between sofa ads by day.

00:12:50.049 --> 00:12:53.049
Tell me about your close encounter.

00:12:53.049 --> 00:12:56.049
Can't share a trade secret. I work for your rival, the Inquisitor.

00:12:56.049 --> 00:12:58.049
Our rival.

00:12:58.049 --> 00:13:00.049
This is the Daily Planet.

00:13:00.049 --> 00:13:02.049
Read in virtually every country across the globe.

00:13:02.049 --> 00:13:04.049
We have no rival.

00:13:04.049 --> 00:13:07.049
It's true. Besides, the planet wouldn't publish a story like that anyway, you know.

00:13:07.049 --> 00:13:12.049
See, that's the kind of Old Guard thinking that's putting newspapers in the crapper all around this country.

00:13:12.049 --> 00:13:16.049
Since when is truth in journalism old guard?

00:13:16.049 --> 00:13:18.049
Well, she says it's true. I believe her.

00:13:18.049 --> 00:13:26.289
I'll tell you what. You deliver me your spaceship story, a story that'll sell papers, and you've got yourself a job here.

00:13:26.289 --> 00:13:28.990
Are you serious?

00:13:28.990 --> 00:13:29.990
You're serious?

00:13:29.990 --> 00:13:30.990
I sound like I'm joking?

00:13:30.990 --> 00:13:49.720
You can't be Khalel.

00:13:49.720 --> 00:13:54.720
He's a sweet chubby baby who laughed when he tickled his feet.

00:13:54.720 --> 00:13:55.720
You knew me on Krypton?

00:13:55.720 --> 00:13:58.720
Yeah, I used to watch over you.

00:13:58.720 --> 00:14:00.720
I don't understand.

00:14:00.720 --> 00:14:02.720
I mean, I left the planet right after you.

00:14:02.720 --> 00:14:03.720
We were on the same trajectory.

00:14:03.720 --> 00:14:07.870
Your ship.

00:14:07.870 --> 00:14:09.870
It seemed to be underwater for a long time.

00:14:09.870 --> 00:14:11.870
You must have crashed landed during the meteor shower,

00:14:11.870 --> 00:14:13.870
into the reservoir.

00:14:13.870 --> 00:14:15.870
When the dam broke, it finally brought you to the surface.

00:14:15.870 --> 00:14:20.399
How long was I in suspended animation?

00:14:20.399 --> 00:14:22.399
animation?

00:14:22.399 --> 00:14:23.399
18 years.

00:14:23.399 --> 00:14:28.799
My embedded learning programs covered a lot of scenarios,

00:14:28.799 --> 00:14:34.940
but this clearly wasn't one of them.

00:14:34.940 --> 00:14:38.509
Kara, why are you searching for me?

00:14:38.509 --> 00:14:41.509
My father, Zorel, told me to find you.

00:14:41.509 --> 00:14:43.509
That was my mission.

00:14:43.509 --> 00:14:45.509
Zorrel?

00:14:45.509 --> 00:14:47.509
and Jorel are brothers.

00:14:47.509 --> 00:14:50.509
Then that makes us...

00:14:50.509 --> 00:14:53.509
Cousins.

00:14:53.509 --> 00:14:55.509
Jerell never mentioned your dad.

00:14:55.509 --> 00:14:57.509
I'll never mentioned your dad.

00:14:57.509 --> 00:15:04.990
He and his brother never talked.

00:15:04.990 --> 00:15:06.490
The house of Vell has a lot of family secrets

00:15:06.490 --> 00:15:10.799
that nobody ever discussed.

00:15:10.799 --> 00:15:15.460
As humans would say, we were dysfunctional.

00:15:15.460 --> 00:15:20.659
Look, I'm sure you have a lot of questions.

00:15:20.659 --> 00:15:23.659
But right now, we need to find my ship.

00:15:23.659 --> 00:15:26.659
I do it myself, but those green rocks, they keep weakening me.

00:15:26.659 --> 00:15:29.659
And trust me, you want to stay away from them.

00:15:29.659 --> 00:15:33.320
If you're around them too long, they can't kill you.

00:15:33.320 --> 00:15:38.200
Kill me.

00:15:38.200 --> 00:15:40.200
Zarel told me that the yellow sun would give me abilities

00:15:40.200 --> 00:15:42.200
behind my wild streams, but...

00:15:42.200 --> 00:15:45.200
He definitely never mentioned any fatal weaknesses.

00:15:45.200 --> 00:15:47.200
It's because he didn't know.

00:15:47.200 --> 00:15:49.200
The green rocks, they're called kryptonite.

00:15:49.200 --> 00:15:52.200
Radioactive pieces of our homeworld.

00:15:52.200 --> 00:15:59.169
How did pieces of Krypton travel 23 galaxies?

00:15:59.169 --> 00:16:03.600
I don't know what happened after you left.

00:16:03.600 --> 00:16:07.600
Well, I know we were in the midst of a global civil war, led by General Zod.

00:16:07.600 --> 00:16:10.600
Zoral told me that Krypton salvation was on Earth,

00:16:10.600 --> 00:16:12.600
and that you and I were the key.

00:16:12.600 --> 00:16:15.750
Hope we're not too late.

00:16:15.750 --> 00:16:20.919
Care, Krypton is gone.

00:16:20.919 --> 00:16:32.419
It exploded.

00:16:32.419 --> 00:16:33.419
You and I...

00:16:33.419 --> 00:16:41.720
We're the only survivors.

00:16:41.720 --> 00:16:43.720
Planets don't just explode, Kalal.

00:16:43.720 --> 00:16:54.000
Ours did.

00:16:54.000 --> 00:17:04.109
This yellow sun has fried your brain cells.

00:17:04.109 --> 00:17:09.210
Come on, help me find my ship.

00:17:09.210 --> 00:17:11.210
I can hide it here on your farm.

00:17:11.210 --> 00:17:12.210
Your ship's missing.

00:17:12.210 --> 00:17:18.220
If it's missing, then humans took it.

00:17:18.220 --> 00:17:21.220
Kalal, if anyone but me tries to open that ship,

00:17:21.220 --> 00:17:23.220
it will activate the self-destruct sequence.

00:17:23.220 --> 00:17:27.519
Define self-destruct?

00:17:27.519 --> 00:17:32.250
I think you'd call it something like a...

00:17:32.250 --> 00:17:34.250
Nuclear explosion.

00:17:34.250 --> 00:17:45.279
Outside the perimeter of the...

00:17:45.279 --> 00:17:51.279
All personnel are advised to remain outside of the perimeter of...

00:17:51.279 --> 00:17:57.450
There's no sign of alien life near that site, none whatsoever.

00:17:57.450 --> 00:18:36.670
Open it.

00:18:36.670 --> 00:18:37.670
This temperature rising steadily.

00:18:37.670 --> 00:19:08.509
Begin extraction protocol from prepared to evacuate, and now we don't have a lot of time, people.

00:19:08.509 --> 00:19:11.509
Lane, I had a feeling you worked fast.

00:19:11.509 --> 00:19:13.509
I didn't know you were a lightning bolt.

00:19:13.509 --> 00:19:14.509
You got pages for me?

00:19:14.509 --> 00:19:16.509
Actually, I need to talk to you about that.

00:19:16.509 --> 00:19:17.509
I'm not interested in talk.

00:19:17.509 --> 00:19:19.509
interested in talk. I don't want to read.

00:19:19.509 --> 00:19:22.509
Look, Chloe Sullivan should write this story.

00:19:22.509 --> 00:19:24.509
She's already on your staff, and let's face it.

00:19:24.509 --> 00:19:26.509
She can write circles around me.

00:19:26.509 --> 00:19:28.509
I know she's family, Lane.

00:19:28.509 --> 00:19:30.509
But Chloe Sullivan's lost her mojo.

00:19:30.509 --> 00:19:32.509
Now she's just another run-of-the-mill hack,

00:19:32.509 --> 00:19:35.509
giving herself carpal tunnel covering City Hall and Fourth of July parades.

00:19:35.509 --> 00:19:38.509
Look, my cousin's feelings mean a lot more to me

00:19:38.509 --> 00:19:39.509
than some stupid article.

00:19:39.509 --> 00:19:42.509
Your cousin's feelings. How sweet.

00:19:42.509 --> 00:19:44.509
Let me tell you something, Lane.

00:19:44.509 --> 00:19:46.509
Newspapers don't have feelings.

00:19:46.509 --> 00:19:47.509
They have feelings.

00:19:47.509 --> 00:19:48.509
They have stories.

00:19:48.509 --> 00:19:50.509
And stories are what pay the bills around here.

00:19:50.509 --> 00:19:52.509
You think I'm being honored by the Publishers Guild tonight

00:19:52.509 --> 00:19:54.509
because I'm Mahatma Gandhi?

00:19:54.509 --> 00:19:56.509
Because I give a damn about feelings?

00:19:56.509 --> 00:19:57.509
No.

00:19:57.509 --> 00:19:58.509
I break stories.

00:19:58.509 --> 00:20:00.509
Any way, anyhow.

00:20:00.509 --> 00:20:05.680
Well, you're going to have to break this one with someone else.

00:20:05.680 --> 00:20:07.680
This isn't about your cousin.

00:20:07.680 --> 00:20:10.680
This so-called flying saucer story, it's all smoke and mirrors.

00:20:10.680 --> 00:20:14.680
You're using some high moral ground to bail out of a sinking ship.

00:20:14.680 --> 00:20:19.410
This ship is far from sunk, Bowtie.

00:20:19.410 --> 00:20:23.809
I happen to have a contact in the Air Force who supplied me with these.

00:20:23.809 --> 00:20:29.410
There's satellite photos showing a caravan of trucks driving from the dam to a grain silo in Granville.

00:20:29.410 --> 00:20:31.410
Does that look like smoke and mirrors to you?

00:20:31.410 --> 00:20:34.410
No. It looks like passion.

00:20:34.410 --> 00:20:36.410
It's what separates you from the rest of the pack.

00:20:36.410 --> 00:20:38.410
This is the fork in your road, Lane.

00:20:38.410 --> 00:20:41.410
In a dozen years, you'll either be Lois Lane,

00:20:41.410 --> 00:20:45.410
Star Reporter whose name is synonymous with the Daily Planet,

00:20:45.410 --> 00:20:48.410
or Lois Fill in the Blank, married to an insurance.

00:20:48.410 --> 00:20:50.910
Married to an insurance adjuster in the sticks,

00:20:50.910 --> 00:20:52.910
with four kids and 40 extra pounds,

00:20:52.910 --> 00:20:54.410
you won't be able to look at a newspaper

00:20:54.410 --> 00:20:57.910
because it'll always remind you of what could have been.

00:20:57.910 --> 00:20:59.910
Which road sounds better to you?

00:20:59.910 --> 00:21:15.569
What do you have for me?

00:21:15.569 --> 00:21:18.069
We applied voice recognition software.

00:21:18.069 --> 00:21:19.569
And using our satellites, cast a net over,

00:21:19.569 --> 00:21:21.569
every landline, the cell phone on the globe.

00:21:21.569 --> 00:21:23.069
I don't care how wide you net is.

00:21:23.069 --> 00:21:25.569
If you don't find lawn, it's not worth a string it's made of.

00:21:25.569 --> 00:21:27.569
We have a match, sir. She's in Asia.

00:21:27.569 --> 00:21:29.569
Where?

00:21:29.569 --> 00:21:30.569
China.

00:21:30.569 --> 00:21:32.569
Our GPS puts her just a few miles from central Shanghai.

00:21:32.569 --> 00:21:35.779
Central Shanghai.

00:21:35.779 --> 00:21:37.779
Prepare the jet for take off.

00:21:37.779 --> 00:21:38.779
Yes, sir.

00:21:38.779 --> 00:21:54.789
Those doors would have opened if you had just waited.

00:21:54.789 --> 00:21:57.789
We don't have time to wait for ancient technology.

00:21:57.789 --> 00:22:00.789
Between the two of us, we can cover more ground.

00:22:00.789 --> 00:22:03.789
Of course, it would help if you could defy gravity.

00:22:03.789 --> 00:22:06.789
Explain to me again why you can't fly?

00:22:06.789 --> 00:22:09.140
I'm not sure.

00:22:09.140 --> 00:22:11.140
Guess the humans are right, Collelle.

00:22:11.140 --> 00:22:14.140
Girls do mature faster than boys.

00:22:14.140 --> 00:22:17.140
It's Clark, remember?

00:22:17.140 --> 00:22:21.630
Start walking. Don't look back.

00:22:21.630 --> 00:22:28.069
I should.

00:22:28.069 --> 00:22:34.400
I've known you were Clark's cousin from all the primary colors.

00:22:34.400 --> 00:22:36.400
Do you know where my ship is?

00:22:36.400 --> 00:22:38.400
Kelle's getting me nowhere.

00:22:38.400 --> 00:22:43.079
It's Clark.

00:22:43.079 --> 00:22:46.079
We've checked every Luther Court facility in the area.

00:22:46.079 --> 00:22:47.079
Do you have any leads?

00:22:47.079 --> 00:22:50.079
Unfortunately, not too many extraterrestrial vehicles

00:22:50.079 --> 00:22:52.079
are actually registered at the DMV.

00:22:52.079 --> 00:22:54.079
I have nothing.

00:22:54.079 --> 00:22:56.079
I told you coming here was a waste of time.

00:22:56.079 --> 00:22:58.079
She's just a human.

00:22:58.079 --> 00:23:01.079
A human who's smarter than both of us combined.

00:23:01.079 --> 00:23:06.130
Look, I'm sorry, Clark, but this new editor is breathing down my neck.

00:23:06.130 --> 00:23:07.130
He wants something.

00:23:07.130 --> 00:23:13.130
big splashy story and all I could come up with is a sudden loss of AMFM radio in Granville.

00:23:13.130 --> 00:23:14.130
I'm out of here.

00:23:14.130 --> 00:23:17.130
I'll just do a flyover and start X-ring every single building.

00:23:17.130 --> 00:23:18.130
Kara, wait.

00:23:18.130 --> 00:23:19.130
Your ship.

00:23:19.130 --> 00:23:21.130
Does it emit any sort of frequency?

00:23:21.130 --> 00:23:24.130
Well, yeah, if it's open, there's an alarm.

00:23:24.130 --> 00:23:27.130
Could that alarm be disrupting the AMFM radios?

00:23:27.130 --> 00:23:33.140
Kolel, if that alarm's been triggered,

00:23:33.140 --> 00:23:35.140
I'm the only one who can disarm it.

00:23:35.140 --> 00:23:48.079
What are we doing up here?

00:23:48.079 --> 00:23:49.079
Time's running out.

00:23:49.079 --> 00:23:50.079
Look, you cover the grounds, I'll get the bird's eye view.

00:23:50.079 --> 00:23:51.079
Get the bird's eye view.

00:23:51.079 --> 00:23:52.079
What's your ship sound like?

00:23:52.079 --> 00:23:56.740
If your ship is submitting an alarm, then you can hear it.

00:23:56.740 --> 00:23:59.740
Even if it's miles away, it's one of our abilities.

00:23:59.740 --> 00:24:00.740
You have to focus.

00:24:00.740 --> 00:24:02.740
Block everything else out.

00:24:02.740 --> 00:24:04.740
Just try.

00:24:04.740 --> 00:24:15.990
All here is the wind.

00:24:15.990 --> 00:24:16.990
Close your eyes, it might help.

00:24:16.990 --> 00:24:21.099
Try to focus.

00:24:21.099 --> 00:24:22.099
I know you can do it.

00:24:22.099 --> 00:24:29.549
Just try to listen to all the sounds around you.

00:24:29.549 --> 00:24:36.000
You can stop.

00:24:36.000 --> 00:24:37.000
Listen, listen.

00:24:37.000 --> 00:24:38.000
I know it's a lot at first.

00:24:38.000 --> 00:24:40.000
You have to focus, okay?

00:24:40.000 --> 00:24:48.470
We need the sounds one by one until all you can do is your ship.

00:24:48.470 --> 00:24:55.619
Come.

00:24:55.619 --> 00:24:57.619
I can hear it.

00:24:57.619 --> 00:25:01.759
And we can find it.

00:25:01.759 --> 00:25:14.410
I knew those roadblocks I slipped past weren't there for just a chemical spill.

00:25:14.410 --> 00:25:18.410
They evacuated the area because what's down here underground.

00:25:18.410 --> 00:25:26.849
And judging by that funky sound and the megawatt light show,

00:25:26.849 --> 00:25:31.849
something's going on behind that door and it's not Lysarium.

00:25:31.849 --> 00:25:50.670
Oh my God.

00:25:50.670 --> 00:25:54.500
It's official.

00:25:54.500 --> 00:25:56.500
I found the Holy Grail.

00:25:56.500 --> 00:26:39.609
Are you okay?

00:26:39.609 --> 00:26:50.180
What are you gonna do?

00:26:50.180 --> 00:27:12.589
Just let you walk away.

00:27:12.589 --> 00:27:19.690
The last time you'll ever touch me.

00:27:19.690 --> 00:27:21.690
If you really think I could just let you walk away.

00:27:21.690 --> 00:27:24.690
What are you going to do, Lex?

00:27:24.690 --> 00:28:06.099
I'm impressed.

00:28:06.099 --> 00:28:08.099
I did learn from the master.

00:28:08.099 --> 00:28:12.309
As soon as I heard you'd freeze yourself,

00:28:12.309 --> 00:28:15.309
I laid out the breadcrumbs and waited for the wolf to come knocking.

00:28:15.309 --> 00:28:18.619
Tell me, Lex.

00:28:18.619 --> 00:28:21.619
How are you planning on getting your revenge?

00:28:21.619 --> 00:28:22.619
Bono.

00:28:22.619 --> 00:28:26.619
If I wanted revenge, we wouldn't be having this conversation.

00:28:26.619 --> 00:28:30.700
I'm here to beg for your forgiveness.

00:28:30.700 --> 00:28:33.700
With a gun pointed at your head, you'll say anything, won't you?

00:28:33.700 --> 00:28:36.700
The things I did to you are beyond inexcusable.

00:28:36.700 --> 00:28:39.700
I don't blame you for wanting to ruin my life.

00:28:39.700 --> 00:28:42.700
I probably would have done the same thing.

00:28:42.700 --> 00:28:44.700
Only not as elegantly.

00:28:44.700 --> 00:28:47.700
I always knew you were smart, Lana.

00:28:47.700 --> 00:28:54.140
I didn't know you were brilliant, using my own science against me.

00:28:54.140 --> 00:28:56.140
It wasn't science, Lex.

00:28:56.140 --> 00:28:59.140
It was your own psychosis.

00:28:59.140 --> 00:29:04.400
You cloned me.

00:29:04.400 --> 00:29:10.369
Not exactly.

00:29:10.369 --> 00:29:13.369
Model 503 was never alive.

00:29:13.369 --> 00:29:24.779
That's why you were able to wield it out of my lab

00:29:24.779 --> 00:29:26.779
and placed in your driver's seat.

00:29:26.779 --> 00:29:34.509
At the time the car exploded,

00:29:34.509 --> 00:29:39.509
you were safe and sound while Model 503 with your DNA

00:29:39.509 --> 00:29:41.509
was being blown to bits.

00:29:41.509 --> 00:29:43.509
It was perfect.

00:29:43.509 --> 00:29:45.509
As far as the world's concerned,

00:29:45.509 --> 00:29:46.509
Lana Luther is dead and buried.

00:29:46.509 --> 00:29:47.509
is dead and buried.

00:29:47.509 --> 00:29:50.509
And a dead woman can't be convicted of murder.

00:29:50.509 --> 00:29:55.500
You'll never hurt another person again, Lex.

00:29:55.500 --> 00:30:04.920
Don't come any closer.

00:30:04.920 --> 00:30:06.920
I want to give you a better target.

00:30:06.920 --> 00:30:08.920
After all the pain I put you through,

00:30:08.920 --> 00:30:10.920
I deserve to die.

00:30:10.920 --> 00:30:13.920
Please, Lord, for the trigger.

00:30:13.920 --> 00:30:20.680
I promise you, the world will be a better place to do it.

00:30:20.680 --> 00:30:58.980
If you want to come back to Smallville, you'll be safe.

00:30:58.980 --> 00:31:00.980
I'll take care of everything.

00:31:01.980 --> 00:31:03.980
You can live your life however you want.

00:31:04.980 --> 00:31:07.980
My father's gone, presumed deadness for me.

00:31:07.980 --> 00:31:10.980
I would never, ever hurt you again.

00:31:10.980 --> 00:31:52.640
Bishop got me were two concussions and a fried room camcorder.

00:31:52.640 --> 00:31:54.640
You were right. I never should have chased that story.

00:31:54.640 --> 00:31:56.640
I tried to warn you, Lois.

00:31:56.640 --> 00:32:00.640
When you're scaling the wall of weird, there aren't any mattresses to break your fall.

00:32:00.640 --> 00:32:02.640
I think I could have landed a job at the daily planet.

00:32:02.640 --> 00:32:03.640
What a joke.

00:32:03.640 --> 00:32:06.640
I have no Chloe Sullivan and never will be.

00:32:06.640 --> 00:32:10.640
Lane, I just read your story. It's ridiculous.

00:32:10.640 --> 00:32:12.640
Well, it was just your first draft, Mr. Gator.

00:32:12.640 --> 00:32:14.640
It's absurd how good it is.

00:32:14.640 --> 00:32:17.640
Your prose leaps off the page like a Bengal tiger.

00:32:17.640 --> 00:32:19.640
I was riveted.

00:32:19.640 --> 00:32:20.640
So you're actually gonna run it?

00:32:20.640 --> 00:32:22.640
Absolutely not. It's utterly unprintable.

00:32:22.640 --> 00:32:24.640
I don't care if every word of it's true.

00:32:24.640 --> 00:32:28.640
I can't run a story about a ship from outer space without a photo.

00:32:28.640 --> 00:32:31.640
You gotta learn, Lane. Always carry a backup camera.

00:32:31.640 --> 00:32:32.640
She's just starting out.

00:32:32.640 --> 00:32:34.640
If you would just give her a second chance...

00:32:34.640 --> 00:32:36.640
You like water, Lane?

00:32:36.640 --> 00:32:38.640
As much as the next girl.

00:32:38.640 --> 00:32:39.640
Because I'm giving you a waterfront view.

00:32:39.640 --> 00:32:40.640
front view.

00:32:40.640 --> 00:32:43.640
This is your new desk right here, right across from cousin Chloe.

00:32:43.640 --> 00:32:44.640
Excuse me?

00:32:44.640 --> 00:32:47.640
If you're lucky, Sullivan, some of her passion will rub off on you.

00:32:47.640 --> 00:32:50.640
Maybe put a little fire on that torch you let burn out after high school.

00:32:50.640 --> 00:32:56.589
Am I hearing things or did you just offer me a job?

00:32:56.589 --> 00:32:58.589
Welcome to the Daily Planet, Lois Lane.

00:32:58.589 --> 00:33:01.589
You play your cards right, you'll be out of this basement quicker and your cousin.

00:33:01.589 --> 00:33:05.589
Nothing like a little family rivalry to keep the bullpen hopping.

00:33:05.589 --> 00:33:27.259
You okay?

00:33:27.259 --> 00:33:40.849
How did it happen?

00:33:40.849 --> 00:33:41.849
Krypton?

00:33:41.849 --> 00:33:45.950
I mean...

00:33:45.950 --> 00:33:50.339
I don't know.

00:33:50.339 --> 00:33:52.339
We always heard whispers of a doomsday scenario,

00:33:52.339 --> 00:33:54.339
but...

00:33:54.339 --> 00:33:56.339
I never thought anyone would actually do it.

00:33:56.339 --> 00:34:03.420
We were supposed to be the most advanced civilization

00:34:03.420 --> 00:34:06.980
in the galaxy.

00:34:06.980 --> 00:34:10.980
One thing I've learned is that evil exists in all cultures

00:34:10.980 --> 00:34:12.980
or how advanced they are.

00:34:12.980 --> 00:34:18.739
Maybe if I had had my abilities on Krypton, I could have saved you.

00:34:18.739 --> 00:34:21.739
You saved a lot of people here today.

00:34:21.739 --> 00:34:24.739
You should feel good about that.

00:34:24.739 --> 00:34:25.739
It's...

00:34:25.739 --> 00:34:26.739
It's different for you.

00:34:26.739 --> 00:34:30.739
You don't have any memory of Krypton.

00:34:30.739 --> 00:34:34.059
This has always been your own.

00:34:34.059 --> 00:34:41.599
Well, then be my memory. Tell me about my family.

00:34:41.599 --> 00:34:45.739
It's hazy.

00:34:45.739 --> 00:34:48.739
And all those years asleep in the ship.

00:34:48.739 --> 00:34:50.739
I do remember some.

00:34:50.739 --> 00:34:59.090
I used to, uh, sneak away from Canber and come and see Lara.

00:34:59.090 --> 00:35:01.090
She always made me smile.

00:35:01.090 --> 00:35:05.460
You knew my mom?

00:35:05.460 --> 00:35:07.460
The day she found out she was pregnant.

00:35:07.460 --> 00:35:10.460
I'd never seen her so happy.

00:35:10.460 --> 00:35:13.179
I'm so cute.

00:35:13.179 --> 00:35:15.659
You were.

00:35:15.659 --> 00:35:24.019
You were a miracle baby.

00:35:24.019 --> 00:35:26.019
Now she's gone.

00:35:26.019 --> 00:35:28.019
My parents are gone.

00:35:28.019 --> 00:35:30.019
The entire house of Elle.

00:35:30.019 --> 00:35:36.059
I'll never see any of my family ever again.

00:35:36.059 --> 00:35:47.789
You're family now.

00:35:47.789 --> 00:35:52.099
Look, you can stay here with me.

00:35:52.099 --> 00:35:56.690
On the farm as long as you want.

00:35:56.690 --> 00:35:58.690
You know, these humans are not as bad as you think.

00:35:58.690 --> 00:36:08.400
Thank you, Collelle.

00:36:08.400 --> 00:36:10.400
I mean, Clark.

00:36:10.400 --> 00:36:18.800
I wish I didn't feel like such a failure.

00:36:18.800 --> 00:36:21.800
I made my father a promise and I couldn't keep it.

00:36:21.800 --> 00:36:22.800
Care, that wasn't your fault.

00:36:22.800 --> 00:36:23.800
That wasn't your fault.

00:36:23.800 --> 00:36:26.800
We can't always be everything our fathers expect us to be.

00:36:26.800 --> 00:36:27.800
I know that firsthand.

00:36:27.800 --> 00:36:29.800
The way he spoke of the crystal.

00:36:29.800 --> 00:36:33.800
He told me to guard it with my life, and now it's gone.

00:36:33.800 --> 00:36:38.750
There was a crystal in that ship?

00:36:38.750 --> 00:36:42.750
With all of my directives and the power to help me along the way.

00:36:42.750 --> 00:36:45.750
If that crystal fell into the wrong hands,

00:36:45.750 --> 00:36:48.750
it could be disastrous.

00:36:48.750 --> 00:36:51.750
Luckily, we don't have to worry about that since it was destroyed with the ship.

00:36:51.750 --> 00:36:53.750
Oh.

00:36:53.750 --> 00:36:54.750
That explosion.

00:36:54.750 --> 00:36:56.750
wouldn't scratch the crystal.

00:36:56.750 --> 00:36:59.750
Only a Kryptonian can destroy it.

00:36:59.750 --> 00:37:01.750
I've searched everywhere.

00:37:01.750 --> 00:37:05.670
That crystal is gone.

00:37:05.670 --> 00:37:30.079
The spacecraft was eviscerated.

00:37:30.079 --> 00:37:58.289
But all was not lost.

00:37:58.289 --> 00:38:00.289
Carlel, my son,

00:38:00.289 --> 00:38:03.289
you have finally chosen to start your training.

00:38:03.289 --> 00:38:07.289
The Kryptonian girl showed up at my doorstep.

00:38:07.289 --> 00:38:09.289
Your name is Kara.

00:38:09.289 --> 00:38:13.920
Last time that happened, you were behind him.

00:38:13.920 --> 00:38:14.920
I know nothing of her around.

00:38:14.920 --> 00:38:16.920
Nothing of her arrival.

00:38:16.920 --> 00:38:20.920
She said she was sent here by her father, Zorel.

00:38:20.920 --> 00:38:23.920
You might remember him since he's your brother.

00:38:23.920 --> 00:38:28.199
Care to tell me why you ignored that branch of the family tree?

00:38:28.199 --> 00:38:34.199
Whatever Zorrel wanted with you, it was not for the greater good of Krypton.

00:38:34.199 --> 00:38:38.199
He could not be trusted, and neither can his daughter.

00:38:38.199 --> 00:38:41.199
You can't blame Kara for the actions of her father.

00:38:41.199 --> 00:38:43.199
She's not here to cause any harm.

00:38:43.199 --> 00:38:45.199
That is an emotional human reaction.

00:38:45.199 --> 00:38:46.199
That is an emotional human reaction.

00:38:46.199 --> 00:38:49.199
Be careful of your feelings, Collelle.

00:38:49.199 --> 00:38:51.199
They can betray you.

00:38:51.199 --> 00:38:57.050
My feelings are part of who I am, whether you like it or not.

00:38:57.050 --> 00:38:59.050
Now what about my training?

00:38:59.050 --> 00:39:02.050
Your training starts with Kira.

00:39:02.050 --> 00:39:05.050
Watch over her, Carlisle.

00:39:05.050 --> 00:39:09.050
She poses a greater threat than you believe.

00:39:09.050 --> 00:39:21.880
Mr. Luther, I take you to find who you were looking for.

00:39:21.880 --> 00:39:25.670
There's someone else I need you to locate.

00:39:25.670 --> 00:39:36.539
This drawing isn't much to go on, sir.

00:39:36.539 --> 00:39:37.539
That's all I have.

00:39:37.539 --> 00:39:41.500
That woman saved my life.

00:39:41.500 --> 00:39:45.869
Use whatever resources are necessary to find her.

00:39:45.869 --> 00:39:49.280
Is that clear?

00:39:49.280 --> 00:39:50.280
Yes, sir.

